            "text": "{\"findings\":[{\"tipo\":\"GPU\",\"causa_raiz\":\"A carga de processamento na GPU atingiu 28.27ms, ultrapassando criticamente o orcamento de 16.7ms para 60 FPS (69 violacoes registradas). Com draw calls dentro do limite (964 de 2579), o gargalo reside na taxa de preenchimento (fillrate), sombreamento complexo de pixels (overdraw/fragment shaders pesados) ou resolucao de renderizacao nativa excessiva para a GTX 1650 sob carga combinada com picos de Garbage Collector.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\nusing UnityEngine.Rendering;\\\\n\\\\npublic class AdaptiveGpuPerformanceManager : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    [Header(\\\\\\\"GPU Throttle Settings\\\\\\\")]\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float targetFrameTimeMs = 16.0f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float minRenderScale = 0.65f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float maxRenderScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float scaleStep = 0.05f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float adjustmentInterval = 0.25f;\\\\n\\\\n    private float currentRenderScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    private float timer = 0f;\\\\n    private FrameTiming[] frameTimings = new FrameTiming[1];\\\\n\\\\n    private void Awake()\\\\n    {\\\\n        QualitySettings.vSyncCount = 0;\\\\n        Application.targetFrameRate = 60;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void Update()\\\\n    {\\\\n        timer += Time.unscaledDeltaTime;\\\\n        if (timer \u003c adjustmentInterval) return;\\\\n        timer = 0f;\\\\n\\\\n        FrameTimingManager.CaptureFrameTimings();\\\\n        uint captured = FrameTimingManager.GetLatestTimings(1, frameTimings);\\\\n\\\\n        if (captured \u003e 0)\\\\n        {\\\\n            float gpuMs = (float)frameTimings[0].gpuFrameTime;\\\\n            if (gpuMs \u003c= 0f)\\\\n            {\\\\n                gpuMs = Time.unscaledDeltaTime * 1000f;\\\\n            }\\\\n\\\\n            if (gpuMs \u003e targetFrameTimeMs && currentRenderScale \u003e minRenderScale)\\\\n            {\\\\n                currentRenderScale = Mathf.Clamp(currentRenderScale - scaleStep, minRenderScale, maxRenderScale);\\\\n                ApplyRenderScale(currentRenderScale);\\\\n            }\\\\n            else if (gpuMs \u003c (targetFrameTimeMs - 3.0f) && currentRenderScale \u003c maxRenderScale)\\\\n            {\\\\n                currentRenderScale = Mathf.Clamp(currentRenderScale + scaleStep, minRenderScale, maxRenderScale);\\\\n                ApplyRenderScale(currentRenderScale);\\\\n            }\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void ApplyRenderScale(float scale)\\\\n    {\\\\n        ScalableBufferManager.ResizeBuffers(scale, scale);\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"A placa de video (GPU) esta demorando quase o dobro do tempo permitido para pintar os pixels na tela (28.27ms contra 16.7ms necessarios para 60 FPS). Como a contagem de Draw Calls esta saudavel (964), o problema nao e a quantidade de objetos desenhados, mas sim o peso de pintar cada pixel (resolucao alta, efeitos de pos-processamento ou sombras complexas). O script implementado monitora os milissegundos da GPU sem gerar lixo de memoria (zero GC) e ajusta a resolucao interna dinamicamente para aliviar a placa de video instantaneamente em momentos de sobrecarga.\"},{\"tipo\":\"GC\",\"causa_raiz\":\"Ocorrencia de coleta de lixo gerando travamento de 5.60ms (gc_collect_ms) devido a alocacao excessiva por frame (96KB no frame amostrado), competindo com a CPU e atrasando a submissao de comandos para a GPU.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\n\\\\npublic class NonAllocBufferUtility : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    private static readonly RaycastHit[] HitBuffer = new RaycastHit[16];\\\\n    private static readonly Collider[] OverlapBuffer = new Collider[32];\\\\n\\\\n    public static int QuerySurroundingsNonAlloc(Vector3 origin, float radius, LayerMask layerMask)\\\\n    {\\\\n        return Physics.OverlapSphereNonAlloc(origin, radius, OverlapBuffer, layerMask);\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public static int RaycastNonAlloc(Ray ray, float distance, LayerMask layerMask)\\\\n    {\\\\n        return Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(ray, HitBuffer, distance, layerMask);\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"Quando o jogo cria variaveis temporarias no Update (como arrays de fisica ou textos repetidos), a Unity precisa acionar o Coletor de Lixo (GC). Esse processo congela a execucao por 5.6ms para limpar a memoria. A solucao e reutilizar buffers pre-alocados (NonAlloc) em vez de criar novas listas a cada quadro, eliminando completamente esses congelamentos.\"}],\"dicas_level_design\":null}",
